<Base lang="en" title="eDistrict UP Status Check & Certificate Verification" description="UP eDistrict tracking, status meanings, certificate verification, safe download, pending payments and complaint escalation." path="/en/status-verification/" altPath="/status-verification/" faqs={faqs} updated="27 October 2026" datePublished="2026-10-23" dateModified="2026-10-27" howto={howto}>
<div class="content-col"><h1 class="page-title">Application Status & Certificate Verification</h1><p class="note">Note: This is an independent information guide — it is not the official portal (edistrict.up.gov.in).</p><p class="updated-line">The correct route for tracking, verification and download</p>
<div class="action-grid"><a class="action-card" href="https://edistrict.up.gov.in/" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Official eDistrict portal ↗</strong><span>Open status or verification</span></a><a class="action-card" href="https://esathi.up.gov.in/citizenservices/login/login.aspx" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Official citizen login ↗</strong><span>Download an issued document</span></a></div>
<section class="box"><h2>Choose the right task</h2><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Keep ready</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Track progress</td><td>Your SRN (Service Request Number)</td><td>Application Status</td></tr><tr><td>Authenticate a certificate</td><td>The Certificate Number printed on the certificate</td><td>Certificate Verification</td></tr><tr><td>Download final PDF</td><td>Citizen credentials</td><td>Issued/Completed Applications</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note">The SRN and the Certificate Number are different numbers and are not interchangeable: the SRN tracks an application, the Certificate Number verifies an issued certificate. Follow the official field label on the portal.</div></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Track step by step</h2><ol><li>Open Application Status on the official portal.</li><li>Enter the receipt/SMS number exactly.</li><li>Read the date, department, pending officer and remarks.</li><li>Save the result privately; do not post personal data publicly.</li><li>If no result appears, recheck the number and obtain a readable CSC receipt.</li></ol></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Common status meanings</h2><table class="data"><tbody><tr><th>Submitted</th><td>The form was received; preserve the receipt.</td></tr><tr><th>Under Verification</th><td>Departmental or field checks are underway.</td></tr><tr><th>Query/Correction</th><td>Fix the exact remark and resubmit where offered.</td></tr><tr><th>Rejected</th><td>Read the reason; file fresh only when instructed.</td></tr><tr><th>Approved</th><td>A decision exists; document generation may be separate.</td></tr><tr><th>Certificate Generated</th><td>Download the signed document.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Verify an issued certificate</h2><ol><li>Open Certificate Verification from the official homepage.</li><li>Enter the Certificate Number printed on the certificate, and any other identifiers the form asks for, exactly as labelled.</li><li>Compare name, issuing authority, date and details.</li><li>Confirm that any QR code opens a government domain.</li><li>Take mismatches to the issuing tehsil/registrar.</li></ol><div class="warn">No record alone does not prove fraud; a wrong field, migrated record or outage can cause it.</div><p>The national <a href="https://dc.crsorgi.gov.in/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Civil Registration System</a> lists Uttar Pradesh among supported states for birth/death records.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Download and store safely</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Use the final signed document from Issued/Completed Applications.</li><li>Prefer the portal download control to browser print.</li><li>Do not edit the original PDF; keep protected cloud and offline backups.</li><li>Check the receiving institution's issue-date and format rules.</li><li>Rely on DigiLocker only when the record appears from the official issuer.</li></ul></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/login-registration/">eSathi Login &amp; Registration</a> — register, log in and fix OTP, captcha and password problems.</li><li><a href="/en/csc-guide/">CSC / Jan Seva Kendra Guide</a> — charges, how to find a centre and safety rules.</li><li><a href="/en/income-certificate/">Income Certificate UP</a> — documents, fees and the online application.</li><li><a href="/en/caste-certificate/">Caste Certificate UP</a> — SC/ST and OBC Non-Creamy Layer certificates.</li><li><a href="/en/domicile-certificate/">Domicile Certificate UP</a> — residence proof for state admissions and jobs.</li></ul></section></div></Base>
